Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:30:42 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1409/1463] HERESY 1457: the LoRA row: a chord and a wave
 instead of the words, the sliders starting alike; the name's column half as
 wide, whole on hover; the budget as two modes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Viktor 15.10.2026, his screenshot of two LoRAs in order: «Три кнопки ВЫКЛ / В ДОЛЮ / ПО ПОРЯДКУ… А ВЫКЛ что делает? Режимов у нас же два? Тогда ВЫКЛ и не нужен»; «Выровняй начальную точку ползунков»; «svg иконки с подсказкой по наведению. Для музыки аккордная svg, для звука — звуковая волна»; «колонку с названием адаптера можно ужать вдвое, обрезать троеточием… при наведении мышью распахивать в полную длину, не смещая дизайн». The budget is Share and In order; none lit is no budget (each adapter at its own strength), the lit one pressed again lets it go. Each half's strength opens with an icon of one width (a chord of three heads on a stem for the music half, Lucide's audio-waveform for the sound half; their tips and the strength's own tip name the half), so both sliders of a row and all rows start and end alike in every language. The name's column 0.42fr (was 0.85fr), cut with an ellipsis, its trigger word too; the whole name over the row on hover (.coll-fullname, as the Librarian's workspaces of 1105), gone on leaving or scrolling. The new tip in all eleven catalogs. Kitchen suite 814/0 (lr57 new; lw47 and lr53 now turn the budget off by pressing the lit mode).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
